```catala-metadata
declaration structure Household:
  data status content Status
  data weekly_income content decimal
  data has_dependants content boolean

declaration enumeration Status:
  -- Pensioner
  -- Carer
  -- Other

#[description = "A household qualifies unless its weekly income exceeds the cap."]
declaration scope Qualifies:
  input h content Household
  output qualifies condition

declaration scope IsAPriorityHousehold:
  input h content Household
  output is_a_priority_household condition

declaration scope Allowance:
  input h content Household
  output allowance content decimal

#[description = "One row of the exhaustive truth table for `qualifies`."]
declaration structure QualifiesEqvRow:
  data p_0 content boolean
  data p_1 content boolean

#[description = "Mode A (boolean reference) rendering of `qualifies`."]
declaration scope QualifiesEqvModeA:
  input row content QualifiesEqvRow
  output verdict condition

#[description = "Mode B (exception ladder) rendering of `qualifies`."]
declaration scope QualifiesEqvModeB:
  input row content QualifiesEqvRow
  output verdict condition

#[description = "True when both renderings agree on this row."]
declaration scope QualifiesEqvAgree:
  input row content QualifiesEqvRow
  output agree content boolean

#[description = "Exhaustive 4-row agreement grid for `qualifies`."]
#[test] declaration scope QualifiesEqvGrid:
  output all_agree content boolean

#[description = "One row of the exhaustive truth table for `allowance`."]
declaration structure AllowanceEqvRow:
  data p_0 content boolean
  data p_1 content boolean

#[description = "Mode A (boolean reference) rendering of `allowance`."]
declaration scope AllowanceEqvModeA:
  input row content AllowanceEqvRow
  output value content decimal

#[description = "Mode B (exception ladder) rendering of `allowance`."]
declaration scope AllowanceEqvModeB:
  input row content AllowanceEqvRow
  output value content decimal

#[description = "True when both renderings agree on this row."]
declaration scope AllowanceEqvAgree:
  input row content AllowanceEqvRow
  output agree content boolean

#[description = "Exhaustive 4-row agreement grid for `allowance`."]
#[test] declaration scope AllowanceEqvGrid:
  output all_agree content boolean

#[description = "Test 1, from the L4 directive at statute.l4:46:1-99."]
#[test] declaration scope Test1:
  output result content decimal

#[description = "Test 2, from the L4 directive at statute.l4:47:1-96."]
#[test] declaration scope Test2:
  output result content boolean
```

## Eligibility for the winter allowance

### Section 1 — the qualifying condition

#### `qualifies`

A household qualifies unless its weekly income exceeds the cap.

Subject to subsection (2), a household qualifies for the allowance if


*Source: s1(1).*

```catala
scope Qualifies:
  label qualifies_p0 rule qualifies
    under condition
      (true and ((output of IsAPriorityHousehold with { -- h: h }).is_a_priority_household or h.has_dependants))
    consequence fulfilled

  exception qualifies_p0 rule qualifies
    under condition
      (h.weekly_income > 400.0)
    consequence not fulfilled
```

### Equivalence check for `qualifies`

The rule above is emitted as an exception ladder (Mode B). The scopes below
re-run both renderings — the ladder and the boolean reference form Mode A —
over every one of the 4 truth assignments to its 2 atomic conditions,
and `QualifiesEqvGrid` fails if they ever disagree. The check is part of the
artifact, so it re-runs on every validation (R4, §8.4).

The atoms, as they appear in the emitted rule:

- `p_0` stands for `(true and ((output of IsAPriorityHousehold with { -- h: h }).is_a_priority_household or h.has_dependants))`
- `p_1` stands for `(h.weekly_income > 400.0)`

```catala
scope QualifiesEqvModeA:
  rule verdict
    under condition
      (row.p_0 and (not row.p_1))
    consequence fulfilled

scope QualifiesEqvModeB:
  label verdict_p0 rule verdict
    under condition
      row.p_0
    consequence fulfilled

  exception verdict_p0 rule verdict
    under condition
      row.p_1
    consequence not fulfilled

scope QualifiesEqvAgree:
  definition agree
    equals
      ((output of QualifiesEqvModeA with { -- row: row }).verdict = (output of QualifiesEqvModeB with { -- row: row }).verdict)

scope QualifiesEqvGrid:
  definition all_agree
    equals
      (for all r among [ QualifiesEqvRow { -- p_0: false -- p_1: false }; QualifiesEqvRow { -- p_0: true -- p_1: false }; QualifiesEqvRow { -- p_0: false -- p_1: true }; QualifiesEqvRow { -- p_0: true -- p_1: true } ] we have (output of QualifiesEqvAgree with { -- row: r }).agree)
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope QualifiesEqvGrid --disable-warnings -F json
{"all_agree":true}
```

#### `is a priority household`

```catala
scope IsAPriorityHousehold:
  # Mode A fallback: no exception ladder is derivable for this rule's shape
  rule is_a_priority_household
    under condition
      (match h.status with pattern -- Pensioner : true -- Carer : true -- Other : false)
    consequence fulfilled
```

### Section 2 — the amount

#### `allowance`


*Source: s2(1).*

```catala
scope Allowance:
  label allowance_r0 definition allowance
    equals
      200.0

  label allowance_r1 exception allowance_r2 definition allowance
    under condition
      (not (output of Qualifies with { -- h: h }).qualifies)
    consequence equals
      0.0

  label allowance_r2 exception allowance_r0 definition allowance
    under condition
      h.has_dependants
    consequence equals
      300.0
```

### Equivalence check for `allowance`

The rule above is emitted as an exception ladder (Mode B). The scopes below
re-run both renderings — the ladder and the boolean reference form Mode A —
over every one of the 4 truth assignments to its 2 atomic conditions,
and `AllowanceEqvGrid` fails if they ever disagree. The check is part of the
artifact, so it re-runs on every validation (R4, §8.4).

The atoms, as they appear in the emitted rule:

- `p_0` stands for `(not (output of Qualifies with { -- h: h }).qualifies)`
- `p_1` stands for `h.has_dependants`

The arms' values are stood in for by pairwise-distinct decimal witnesses.
Catala's exception mechanism does not inspect the value it selects, so the
rewrite is uniform in the consequence type and distinct witnesses make
*which arm won* observable — which is the whole of what the ladder decides.

```catala
scope AllowanceEqvModeA:
  definition value
    equals
      (if row.p_0 then 1.0 else (if row.p_1 then 2.0 else 3.0))

scope AllowanceEqvModeB:
  label value_r0 definition value
    equals
      3.0

  label value_r1 exception value_r2 definition value
    under condition
      row.p_0
    consequence equals
      1.0

  label value_r2 exception value_r0 definition value
    under condition
      row.p_1
    consequence equals
      2.0

scope AllowanceEqvAgree:
  definition agree
    equals
      ((output of AllowanceEqvModeA with { -- row: row }).value = (output of AllowanceEqvModeB with { -- row: row }).value)

scope AllowanceEqvGrid:
  definition all_agree
    equals
      (for all r among [ AllowanceEqvRow { -- p_0: false -- p_1: false }; AllowanceEqvRow { -- p_0: true -- p_1: false }; AllowanceEqvRow { -- p_0: false -- p_1: true }; AllowanceEqvRow { -- p_0: true -- p_1: true } ] we have (output of AllowanceEqvAgree with { -- row: r }).agree)
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope AllowanceEqvGrid --disable-warnings -F json
{"all_agree":true}
```

## Tests

One scope per `#EVAL` / `#ASSERT` directive in the L4 source, with the
arguments the directive supplied. The expected values below were computed
by L4's own evaluator, so `clerk test` compares the two languages rather
than comparing Catala with itself (R7, §8.7).

```catala
scope Test1:
  definition result
    equals
      (output of Allowance with { -- h: Household { -- status: Pensioner -- weekly_income: 100.0 -- has_dependants: true } }).allowance
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Test1 --disable-warnings -F json
{"result":"300"}
```

```catala
scope Test2:
  definition result
    equals
      (output of Qualifies with { -- h: Household { -- status: Other -- weekly_income: 100.0 -- has_dependants: false } }).qualifies
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Test2 --disable-warnings -F json
{"result":false}
```
